// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit) — FIXED as a TYPECHECKER
// unsoundness; kept as a CompileErr-agree regress pin.
// Found by soak jul31a fuzz lane (2026-07-31, first find of the round,
// campaign binary 55df55a2; also reproduces on 73de0cab — pre-existing).
// Pre-fix: compiled, then interp Trace([]) vs jit Trace([0:[]]) — a Fn
// value flowing where List<i64> was typed (each backend improvising on
// a value that contradicts its type; the jul18c ABI-hazard class).
// root_cause: three deliberate mechanisms composing into an admission.
// (1) `let rec f = |n, acc| f` forces 'r := fn(..) -> 'r; the occurs
//     check refuses, leaving 'r open with the non-blocking
//     cycle_refused mark (jul22e).
// (2) list::map's tc0 arg check binds the open poisoned cell rhs-ward
//     to Abstract(list::List) — ordinary HM, poison laundered.
// (3) tc1 static resolution's instance recheck hits Abstract-vs-Fn,
//     classified AbstractOpaque -> RESOLVE-DISCARD to dynamic — and
//     the finite-type rejection (settle_or_bottom) lives only in the
//     terminal settle of RESOLVED sites, so no check remained. The
//     flat (unblocked) form was always rejected: its topology let
//     resolution succeed and reach settle_terminal.
// FIX (Eric-approved 2026-07-31): contains_mismatch refuses the
// AbstractOpaque classification when either compared type reaches an
// open, unconstrained, cycle_refused cell — that failure is the
// infinite type surfacing at a consumer, not opacity; it now rejects
// with the same "cannot infer a finite type" error as the settle path.
// Both modes agree: CompileErr.
{let l = {let rec f = |n, acc| f; f(f64:0., buffer::to_string)}; list::to_array(list::map(l, |x| x * i64:2))}
